1. Install [Miniconda](https://docs.conda.io/en/latest/miniconda.html) if you don't have conda already.
2. [If applicable] Install Zurich Instruments LabOne: [link]
3. Clone this repo:
   git clone https://github.com/you/repo.git
   cd repo
4. Create the environment:
   conda env create -f environment_full.yml
5. Activate it:
   conda activate mfia
6. Run:
   python TCycle.py

   Note that I have opted to just manually change the driving voltage and freq. on the UI because I have not
   had time to edit that part of the code yet.

   zhinstExample is code provided by the company.

   My code makes references to a temperature board, that is for driving my own peltier, and is not necessary for you.